---
import DocPage from '../components/DocPage.astro';
---

<DocPage lang="en" title="ToastKit — SwiftUI toast documentation" description="Build stacked, swipeable toast notifications in SwiftUI with ToastKit.">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><span>DOCUMENTATION</span><span class="crumb-slash">/</span><span>GUIDES</span></div>
    <p class="hero-kicker"><span class="pulse"></span> SWIFTUI · OPEN SOURCE</p>
    <h1>Notifications that<br /><em>feel at home.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">A guide to adding thoughtful, stacked toast notifications to your SwiftUI app — with gestures, timing, and style built in.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary-button" href="/get-started/">Start building <span>↓</span></a><span class="version">iOS 17+ <i>·</i> Swift 5.10</span></div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="glow"></div>
      <div class="toast-card back-card"><span class="mini-icon muted">↻</span><span><b>Sync complete</b><small>Everything is up to date</small></span></div>
      <div class="toast-card front-card"><span class="mini-icon">✓</span><span><b>Changes saved</b><small>Your work is safe and sound.</small></span><span class="spark">✦</span></div>
      <div class="art-caption">A little feedback goes a long way <span>✳</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="doc-section" id="overview">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="section-index">00</span><div><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT OVERVIEW</p><h2>About ToastKit</h2></div></div>
    <p>ToastKit is an open-source SwiftUI library for stacked, swipeable toast notifications in iOS apps. It handles presentation, timing, gestures and accessibility, while styles and themes let you shape the cards to fit your app.</p>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <article><span class="pill neutral">STACK</span><h3>Notifications that stay organized</h3><p>New toasts stack in front, with timing that waits until each card is visible.</p></article>
      <article><span class="pill amber">ACTIONS</span><h3>Gestures with clear choices</h3><p>Tap, swipe, or press and hold to reveal named actions before choosing.</p></article>
      <article><span class="pill neutral">PROGRESS</span><h3>Work with a result</h3><p>Show ongoing work with progress, Cancel and Retry, then turn the same card into its outcome.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Where it is used:</strong> the repository includes <code>ToastKitDemo</code>, a sample iOS app that demonstrates the library. No external adopter projects are currently listed.</p>
    <p>ToastKit supports iOS 17 and later, including iPadOS. It is built for SwiftUI and has no dependencies beyond SwiftUI.</p>
    <div class="callout"><span>↗</span><p><strong>Open source on GitHub.</strong> Browse the source, releases and demo project in the <a href="https://github.com/DavidRicardoWilde/swiftui-toastkit">ToastKit repository</a>.</p></div>
  </section>
</DocPage>
